@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Mutation Baseline v0.1
+
+This note records the accepted mutation-test baseline for residual issues #102
+through #105 after the final #88 run.
+
+## Source Run
+
+- Tool: Togi 0.1.0
+- Command scope:
+  - `crates/opencem-cli/src/commands/pack.rs`
+  - `crates/opencem-cli/src/commands/report.rs`
+  - `crates/opencem-cli/src/evidence.rs`
+  - `crates/opencem-cli/src/paths.rs`
+  - `crates/opencem-core/src/artifacts.rs`
+- Final result: 75 killed, 4 survived, 5 timeout, 8 build errors
+- Saved `.togi-baseline`: 75 killed of 84 comparable mutants
+- Score: 89.3%
+- Duration: 434.96s
+
+## Residual Classification
+
+- #102: pack fallback filename survivors were fixed by replacing defensive
+  fallback strings with an explicit missing-filename error path.
+- #103: the artifact hash buffer mutations from 8192 to 8191 and 8193 are
+  accepted as equivalent behavior. Streaming hash correctness is independent of
+  chunk size.
+- #104: the `current_unix_seconds` fallback mutation from 0 to 1 is accepted as
+  an unreachable clock fallback on supported systems.
+- #104: the metadata read-error `continue` survivor is accepted as a
+  race/permission edge. Testing it deterministically requires a filesystem race.
+- #105: hash loop termination timeouts are expected non-terminating mutants.
+- #105: build errors are non-typechecking mutations and should stay visible in
+  future reports.
+
+## v0.1 Decision
+
+The saved `.togi-baseline` is accepted for v0.1 with the classifications above.
+Future mutation runs should keep build errors and timeouts visible rather than
+hiding them inside the comparable-mutant score.
